{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-9090-1",
  "summary": "apache2 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "Zhenpeng Lin discovered that Apache HTTP Server's mod_dav module\nincorrectly calculated memory sizes when handling WebDAV locks. An attacker\nwith permission to create WebDAV locks could possibly use this issue to\ncause Apache HTTP Server to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-42528)\n\nIt was discovered that Apache HTTP Server's mod_vhost_alias module\nincorrectly handled certain requests, leading to a one-byte stack buffer\noverflow. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Apache\nHTTP Server to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute\narbitrary code. (CVE-2026-109163)\n\nIt was discovered that Apache HTTP Server's mod_md module incorrectly\nhandled certain conditions, leading to a NULL pointer dereference. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause Apache HTTP Server to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu\n20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, and Ubuntu\n26.10. (CVE-2026-106023)\n\nIt was discovered that Apache HTTP Server's mod_http2 module incorrectly\nhandled certain request headers, leading to heap corruption. A remote\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause Apache HTTP Server to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary\ncode. This issue only affected Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu\n24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-119618)\n\nFeliks Penconek, Yang Song, and JiaSheng He discovered that Apache HTTP\nServer could treat the target of some internal redirects from CGI programs\nas a CGI program. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\nexecute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and\nUbuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-42356)",
